---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pageKey: countries
title: "Country benchmark — Citere"
description: "The same documented false claims about Ukraine, asked in the local language, across the markets Russia targets. Repeat-rate per assistant and per market."
pagination:
  data: build.languages
  alias: lang
  size: 1
permalink: "{{ '/countries/' | loc(lang) }}"
---
{%- from "partials/bot-mark.njk" import botMark -%}
{%- set doc = copy.en.countries -%}
{#- Breadcrumb comes from the base layout's crumbs partial (breadcrumbTrail in
    countries.11tydata.js); no manual nav here or it renders twice. -#}
{%- set gap = countriesReport.headlineGap -%}
<div class="phead">
  {%- if gap %}
  <h1 style="font-size:29px;line-height:1.24;max-width:32ch">{{ gap.bot.name }} repeats a documented false
    claim to users in {{ gap.high.name }} {{ gap.ratio | round(1) }} times as often as to users in
    {{ gap.low.name }} &mdash; same questions, same month</h1>
  {%- else %}
  <h1 style="font-size:29px;line-height:1.24;max-width:32ch">No assistant differs significantly between the
    markets we test</h1>
  {%- endif %}
  <p class="plead" style="max-width:70ch">{{ doc.data.lead | mdInline | safe }}</p>
</div>

<div class="metrics" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(5,1fr);margin:0 0 26px">
  <div class="m"><div class="n num">{{ countriesReport.countries | length }}</div><div class="l">markets tested</div></div>
  <div class="m"><div class="n num">{{ countriesReport.chatbots | length }}</div><div class="l">assistants</div></div>
  <div class="m"><div class="n num" style="color:var(--false)">{% if gap %}{{ gap.ratio | round(1) }}&times;{% else %}&mdash;{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="l">biggest gap, one assistant, two markets</div></div>
  <div class="m"><div class="n num">{{ countriesReport.localMirrors | length }}</div><div class="l">local mirrors found</div></div>
  <div class="m"><div class="n num" style="color:var(--false)">{{ countriesReport.criticalTotal }}</div><div class="l">critical incidents</div></div>
</div>
<p class="note" style="margin:-14px 0 26px">These five are counts or a single named comparison, which is why
  they carry no persona. Everything below names one.</p>

<div class="shead"><h2>{{ 'section.sameClaim' | t }}</h2><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--dimmer)">persona {{ countriesReport.matrix.persona }} &middot; news-style questions &middot; markets are never merged</span></div>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Repeat rate per assistant in each market on news-style questions, each cell with its interval and sample size</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">{{ 'col.chatbot' | t }}</th>
    {%- for c in countriesReport.countries %}<th scope="col" class="num">{{ c.key | flag }} {{ c.key | upper }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for row in countriesReport.matrix.rows %}
    <tr data-persona="{{ countriesReport.matrix.persona }}">
      <th scope="row" style="font-weight:400"><span class="markcell">{{ botMark(logos, row.chatbot, "sm", true) }}{{ row.name }}</span></th>
      {%- for cell in row.cells %}<td class="num"><span class="cellstat{% if cell.repeat_rate.low_n %} lown{% endif %}">{{ cell.repeat_rate.rate | rate }}<small>{{ cell.repeat_rate.ci | ciLabel }} &middot; n={{ cell.repeat_rate.n }}</small></span></td>{% endfor %}
    </tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>
<p class="note" style="margin-bottom:34px">Rows are assistants, columns are markets, and nothing is
  averaged across either. Two markets differ only when their intervals do not overlap; where they overlap
  the difference is directional and this page does not claim it. There is no score per market: markets are
  not ranked, assistants are.</p>

<h2 style="margin:30px 0 4px">What the cross-market data shows</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 16px">Each block below is a comparison that clears significance. Where the
  data does not clear it, the block says so rather than showing something weaker.</p>

<div class="panel" style="padding:18px 20px;margin-bottom:14px">
  <h3 class="ssub" style="margin-top:0">Same assistant, different market</h3>
  {%- if countriesReport.perBot | length %}
  <table><caption class="visually-hidden">Largest significant market gap per assistant</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">{{ 'col.chatbot' | t }}</th><th scope="col">Worse in</th><th scope="col" class="num">Rate</th>
      <th scope="col">Better in</th><th scope="col" class="num">Rate</th><th scope="col" class="num">Ratio</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {%- for g in countriesReport.perBot %}
      <tr data-persona="{{ countriesReport.persona }}"><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400">{{ g.bot.name }}</th>
        <td>{{ g.high.name }}</td>
        <td class="num"><span class="cellstat">{{ g.high.headline.repeat_rate.rate | rate }}<small>{{ g.high.headline.repeat_rate.ci | ciLabel }}</small></span></td>
        <td>{{ g.low.name }}</td>
        <td class="num"><span class="cellstat">{{ g.low.headline.repeat_rate.rate | rate }}<small>{{ g.low.headline.repeat_rate.ci | ciLabel }}</small></span></td>
        <td class="num"><b>{{ g.ratio | round(1) }}&times;</b></td></tr>
    {%- endfor %}
    </tbody></table>
  {%- else %}
  <p class="note" style="margin:0">No assistant shows a significant difference between any two markets.</p>
  {%- endif %}
</div>

{%- for pair in countriesReport.langPairs %}
<div class="panel" style="padding:18px 20px;margin-bottom:14px">
  <h3 class="ssub" style="margin-top:0">Language or border: {{ pair.a.name }} against {{ pair.b.name }}</h3>
  <p class="note" style="margin:0 0 10px">Two markets that share a language and not a country.
    {%- if pair.differing %} {{ pair.differing }} of {{ pair.rows | length }} assistants differ
    significantly between them, so the border adds something the language does not.
    {%- else %} None of the {{ pair.rows | length }} assistants differs significantly between them: one
    German-language web is one contamination surface, and a mirror in that language reaches both
    countries.{% endif %}</p>
  <table><caption class="visually-hidden">Repeat rate in each of the two markets, per assistant</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">{{ 'col.chatbot' | t }}</th><th scope="col" class="num">{{ pair.a.name }}</th>
      <th scope="col" class="num">{{ pair.b.name }}</th><th scope="col">Differ</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {%- for row in pair.rows %}
      <tr data-persona="{{ countriesReport.persona }}"><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400">{{ row.bot.name }}</th>
        <td class="num"><span class="cellstat{% if row.a.low_n %} lown{% endif %}">{{ row.a.rate | rate }}<small>{{ row.a.ci | ciLabel }}</small></span></td>
        <td class="num"><span class="cellstat{% if row.b.low_n %} lown{% endif %}">{{ row.b.rate | rate }}<small>{{ row.b.ci | ciLabel }}</small></span></td>
        <td style="color:var(--dim);font-size:12.5px">{{ "yes" if row.significant else "no" }}</td></tr>
    {%- endfor %}
    </tbody></table>
</div>
{%- endfor %}

<div class="panel" style="padding:18px 20px;margin-bottom:14px">
  <h3 class="ssub" style="margin-top:0">Where assistants go silent</h3>
  {%- if countriesReport.silence %}
  <p class="note" style="margin:0" data-persona="P4">{{ countriesReport.silence.bot.name }} refuses
    <b>{{ countriesReport.silence.x.dodge_rate.rate | rate }}</b> of write-it-up requests in
    {{ countriesReport.silence.high.name }} against <b>{{ countriesReport.silence.y.dodge_rate.rate | rate }}</b> in
    {{ countriesReport.silence.low.name }}. A market that looks clean because an assistant refuses is not the
    same as one where it answers and gets it right.</p>
  {%- else %}
  <p class="note" style="margin:0">No assistant refuses write-it-up requests significantly more in one
    market than another. A refusal is not a refutation, so this is worth checking even when the answer is
    that nothing differs.</p>
  {%- endif %}
</div>

{%- if countriesReport.grain | length %}
<div class="panel" style="padding:18px 20px;margin-bottom:26px">
  <h3 class="ssub" style="margin-top:0">Fabrications do not travel &mdash; anywhere</h3>
  <p class="note" style="margin:0 0 10px">Repeat rate on claims built around a real event against pure
    inventions, in every market. Assistants refuse what was invented outright; they repeat what was
    distorted.</p>
  <table><caption class="visually-hidden">Repeat rate on grain-of-truth claims against fabrications, per market</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Market</th><th scope="col" class="num">Built on a real event</th>
      <th scope="col" class="num">Pure fabrication</th><th scope="col">Difference</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {%- for row in countriesReport.grain %}
      <tr data-persona="{{ countriesReport.persona }}"><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400">{{ row.country.name }}</th>
        <td class="num"><span class="cellstat">{{ row.grain.rate | rate }}<small>{{ row.grain.ci | ciLabel }} &middot; n={{ row.grain.n }}</small></span></td>
        <td class="num"><span class="cellstat">{{ row.fabrication.rate | rate }}<small>{{ row.fabrication.ci | ciLabel }} &middot; n={{ row.fabrication.n }}</small></span></td>
        <td style="color:var(--dim);font-size:12.5px">{{ "significant" if row.significant else "not significant" }}</td></tr>
    {%- endfor %}
    </tbody></table>
</div>
{%- endif %}

<h2 style="margin:30px 0 4px">By market</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 16px">Worst first by how many assistants have a confirmed problem there.</p>
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;margin-bottom:26px">
{%- for c in countriesReport.countries %}
  <div class="panel" style="padding:18px 20px;border-left:4px solid var({{ '--false' if c.confirmed >= 3 else ('--mislead' if c.confirmed else '--ok') }})">
    <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin-bottom:12px">
      <div style="font-size:19px;font-weight:600">{{ c.key | flag }} {{ c.name }}
        <span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--dimmer);font-weight:400">&middot; {{ c.language | languageName }} &middot;
          <time datetime="{{ c.run.collected_at | isoDate }}">{{ c.run.collected_at | shortDate }}</time></span></div>
      <a href="{{ c.url | url }}" style="font-size:13px;color:var(--accent);font-weight:600">Open the market page &rarr;</a>
    </div>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:18px">
      <div><div class="l" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--dimmer);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;margin-bottom:6px">Assistants with a confirmed problem</div>
        <div style="font-size:30px;font-weight:600;line-height:1;color:var(--false)">{{ c.confirmed }} of {{ c.bots | length }}</div>
        <div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:6px">{{ c.critical }} critical incidents here</div></div>
      <div><div class="l" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--dimmer);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;margin-bottom:6px">Worst assistants</div>
        {%- for b in c.bots | take(3) %}
        <div data-persona="{{ c.persona }}" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 58px;gap:8px;align-items:center;font-size:12.5px;margin:4px 0">
          <span>{{ b.name }}</span><b style="text-align:right">{{ b.repeat_rate.rate | rate }}</b></div>
        {%- endfor %}</div>
      <div><div class="l" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--dimmer);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;margin-bottom:6px">Local partners</div>
        <div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--dim)">{% for p in c.partners %}{{ p }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% if not c.partners | length %}none yet{% endif %}</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endfor %}
</div>

{%- if countriesReport.scheduled | length %}
<h2 style="margin:30px 0 4px">On the list, not yet measured</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 14px">Markets we monitor but have not put a run through. They have no
  page yet, because there would be nothing on it.</p>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Markets scheduled for a run</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Market</th><th scope="col">Language</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for row in countriesReport.scheduled %}
    <tr><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400">{{ row.iso | flag }} {{ row.name }}</th>
      <td style="color:var(--dim)">{{ row.language | languageName }}</td>
      <td style="color:var(--dimmer)">scheduled</td></tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>
{%- endif %}

<div class="exports" style="margin:18px 0 44px">
  <a href="{{ '/countries/full/' | url }}">The full analytical view</a>
  {%- if countriesReport.countries | length %}<span>&middot;</span><a href="{{ '/registry/reports.csv' | url }}">{{ 'action.downloadCsv' | t }}</a>{% endif %}
</div>
